Changes made for Cubbie (cubbie.ai), 2026-10-20:

- SKILL.md: renamed the skill to cubbie-skill-creator; added Cubbie branches to the
  interview, drafting and test steps; noted Cubbie's install limits for description
  optimization; replaced .skill packaging with publishing to GitHub; added Codex
  notes. The general workflow is otherwise unchanged.
- Added references/cubbie-capabilities.md, references/cubbie-auth.md,
  references/imessage-style.md and references/cubbie-testing.md.
- Added scripts/validate_cubbie_skill.py (Cubbie's install checks, standalone) and
  scripts/github_link.py (prints the pinned GitHub install link).
- Removed scripts/package_skill.py and scripts/quick_validate.py, which built and
  checked .skill archives; the two scripts above replace them.
- Added README.md and this NOTICE.

Updated 2026-10-23 to Cubbie's install rules at that date (descriptions up to 1024
characters, no SKILL.md or references size caps, UTF-8 for every Markdown file, 10 MiB
per Skill, folders of Skills, background logins, run-time website approval, update by
link, reserved exit codes, the 30 MiB archive limit).

Updated 2026-10-24 to Cubbie's install rules at that date: a Skill is a plain folder
copied to the student's drive and cubbie.yaml is no longer read (references/cubbie-yaml.md
removed); setup commands, keys and logins are written in SKILL.md; names and descriptions
are repaired instead of refused; keys reach a command that names them; no install limit.

All other files are unchanged from the source commit.
